p2u: 1
deck:
  title: Raft consensus
  subtitle: Understandable distributed consensus
  theme: violet
  meta:
    venue: Distributed Systems Reading Group
slides:
  - layout: section
    title: Raft
    body: Consensus, made understandable
    notes: Set up the problem. Three parts — leader election, log replication, safety.

  - layout: content
    title: Leader election
    body: |
      A **leader** is elected by a majority of the cluster.

      $$ \text{term} = \text{term} + 1 $$

      - Followers become candidates after an election timeout.
      - A candidate wins with a majority of votes.
    notes: Majority quorum is the key invariant.

  - layout: diagram
    title: Log replication
    body: The leader appends entries and replicates them to followers.
    blocks:
      - kind: diagram
        lang: d2
        source: |
          direction: right
          leader: "Leader" { shape: hexagon }
          follower: "Follower" { shape: cylinder }
          leader -> follower: "AppendEntries"
    notes: An entry is committed once a majority has stored it.

  - layout: equation
    title: Election safety
    blocks:
      - kind: equation
        source: \sum_{i=1}^{n} \mathrm{votes}_i > \frac{n}{2}
    notes: At most one leader per term.